{"title":"Career Roadmap · Vascular Sonographer","role":"Vascular Sonographer","summary":"A Vascular Sonographer is a diagnostic imaging professional who performs and documents non-invasive ultrasound examinations of arteries and veins using B-mode, colour Doppler and spectral Doppler techniques.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Medical Sonography / Ultrasound Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Vascular Sonographer is a diagnostic imaging professional who performs and documents non-invasive ultrasound examinations of arteries and veins using B-mode, colour Doppler and spectral Doppler techniques."},{"type":"h","text":"The role focuses on evaluating:"},{"type":"h","text":"Blood-flow characteristics"},{"type":"h","text":"Vessel anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Vessel patency"},{"type":"h","text":"Stenosis"},{"type":"h","text":"Occlusion"},{"type":"h","text":"Thrombosis"},{"type":"h","text":"Aneurysms"},{"type":"h","text":"Peripheral arterial disease"},{"type":"h","text":"Venous insufficiency"},{"type":"h","text":"Carotid disease"},{"type":"h","text":"Vascular abnormalities"},{"type":"p","text":"Vascular sonographers work closely with radiologists, vascular surgeons, cardiologists, vascular physicians and other healthcare professionals."},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification and scope note","text":"“Vascular Sonographer” is a specialized imaging role. A generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT qualification does not automatically qualify someone to independently perform diagnostic ultrasound examinations. Students targeting this career should pursue a recognized sonography/medical-imaging/vascular-sonography qualification and supervised clinical training appropriate to the jurisdiction and employer. The final diagnostic interpretation is performed by the appropriately authorized physician or specialist."}]},{"heading":"Recomme